    "result_text": "All 70 tests pass, build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on `POST /api/owners` (read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`), returning `true` when any of the three signals holds and `false` otherwise.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `riskFlag` boolean property (readOnly) to the Owner schema. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field, which MapStruct wires automatically.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a derived `getRiskFlag()` getter combining the three conditions with OR:\n   - **possible duplicate** \u2192 reuses the existing `getPossibleDuplicate()`.\n   - **disposable-adjacent email domain** \u2192 new `hasDisposableAdjacentEmail()` helper: the email domain's base label (before the first dot) matches a known disposable domain's base label (`mailinator`/`tempmail`/`guerrillamail`). This catches near-variants under a different TLD (e.g. `mailinator.net`), since exact blocklist matches are already rejected with 400 at create time.\n   - **city over soft capacity** \u2192 reuses `getCapacityWarning()`, which is true when the city already held 40+ owners (the soft threshold below the hard cap of 50).\n\nBecause `getRiskFlag()` is derived purely from stored fields (`possibleDuplicate`, `capacityWarning`, `email`), it computes correctly both on create and on read-back.\n\nThe `Cp58` test (`riskFlag` is `false` for a normal structured owner) passes, and the full suite of 70 tests remains green.",
